diff --git a/application/ui/README.md b/application/ui/README.md
index 42b198ec1f4c33af9bf496a651a7d92202967c2b..91438466ebbd39311c09861ae725caeffb6b878a 100644
--- a/application/ui/README.md
+++ b/application/ui/README.md
@@ -10,6 +10,16 @@ The Geti™ applications aim to provide a user experience and design language co
 - **API Adaptability**: Adapting the UI to REST API changes should require minimal effort.
 - **Consistency**: Maintain a unified look, feel, and user experience across the whole Geti ecosystem through shared design language, architectural patterns, and reusable components.
 
+## Interface language
+
+Choose **简体中文** or **English** from the **Language / 语言** picker in the upper-right corner of the project list, project creation page, or project header. Save any unfinished form before switching: changing the language refreshes the current page so static menu labels and date/number formatting stay consistent.
+
+The app detects the browser language on first use and remembers the selection in local storage (`geti-language`). A `?lng=zh-CN` or `?lng=en` URL parameter takes precedence, including when local storage is unavailable. Traditional Chinese browser locales currently fall back to Simplified Chinese for untranslated messages.
+
+Translations cover project management, datasets, annotation tools, training settings and model descriptions, inference configuration, dialogs, and notifications. Project/label names, filenames, model identifiers, and raw backend diagnostic logs retain their original content.
+
+UI messages use `t` from `src/i18n` and the matching flat English/Simplified Chinese resources in `src/i18n/locales`. Use interpolation for variable values and `Trans` for rich text. Translate backend parameter metadata at the display boundary; never translate API keys, submitted enum values, shortcuts, or user-provided names. New UI copy should have entries in both `en.json` and `zh-CN.json`.
+
 ## 🚀 Quick Start
 
